    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37689" root="لذ" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَللَّذْ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَللَّذِ</span> [thus written with two láms]
dial. forms of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الَّذِى</span>: dual <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اللَّذَا</span>, with the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ن</span>
elided: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الَّذِينَ</span>; and sometimes, in the nom.
case, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الَّذُونَ</span>. (S.) Their proper art. is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لذى</span>.
(IB, K.) [See an ex. in a verse cited voce
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَزَبَّى</span>.]

